msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-MicoAir743-AIO.rst:48
#: d8b49c7a05c5494d9231701911d51273
msgid "RC Input"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-MicoAir743-AIO.rst:49
#: 1e014012e0ec4aaa89da680969bd20c7
msgid "The default RC input is configured on the UART6 RX6 input and can be used for all ArduPilot supported unidirectional receiver protocols. The SBus input on the HD VTX connector is tied to RX6 so disconnect its wire if using RX6 for a different RC receiver."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-MicoAir743-AIO.rst:51
#: 01e97036c85941a4adcbc542f61aa0b0
msgid "PPM is not supported."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-MicoAir743-AIO.rst:52
#: 1140c657af3542d8b3ee89143a063ae0
msgid "SBUS/DSM/SRXL connects to the RX6 pin."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-MicoAir743-AIO.rst:53
#: ec18e3cec2f641b49318f81c46b7379c
msgid "FPort requires connection to TX6 and RX6 via a bi-directional inverter. See :ref:`common-FPort-receivers`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-MicoAir743-AIO.rst:54
#: 0b0062575c934cd7bad0fc52db79481c
msgid "CRSF also requires a TX6 connection, in addition to RX6, and automatically provides telemetry."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-MicoAir743-AIO.rst:55
#: e8daee27ba284f81acc3906fc53c72cb
msgid "SRXL2 requires a connection to TX6 and automatically provides telemetry. Set :ref:`SERIAL5_OPTIONS<SERIAL5_OPTIONS>` to “4”."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-MicoAir743-AIO.rst:58
#: a896cdb64a6b42ed835ed94aab557cb1
msgid "OSD"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-MicoAir743-AIO.rst:59
#: bd0b309577654b00ba38c320c91d89c1
msgid "MicoAir743-AIO supports using its internal OSD using OSD_TYPE 1 (MAX7456 driver). External OSD support such as DJI or DisplayPort can be used simultaneously and is pre-configured on SERIAL2 but can be supported on any spare UART. See :ref:`common-msp-osd-overview-4.2` for more info."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-MicoAir743-AIO.rst:62
#: e52c5a8b77ef4668a5df966f3af7879c
msgid "VTX Support"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-MicoAir743-AIO.rst:64
#: a6087bbdf9d84a4fb2e9ec54ea9244ec
msgid "The SH1.0-6P connector supports a DJI Air Unit / HD VTX connection. Protocol defaults to DisplayPort. Pin 1 of the connector is 12v so be careful not to connect this to a peripheral requiring 5v."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-MicoAir743-AIO.rst:67
#: 0de3bb03897f43c1a541c32194429f2f
msgid "PWM Output"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-MicoAir743-AIO.rst:68
#: 8b1ab7eb3ed743d8b717a44057af264c
msgid "The MicoAir743-AIO supports up to 9 PWM outputs."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-MicoAir743-AIO.rst:70
#: 4f5b83017bd5406b9449521578fc7a03
msgid "All the channels support DShot. Channels 1-8 support bi-directional DShot. PWM outputs are grouped and every group must use the same output protocol:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-MicoAir743-AIO.rst:72
#: b2ce2a855ab54d1280ffacff12386b8d
msgid "1, 2, 3, 4 are Group 1;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-MicoAir743-AIO.rst:73
#: a3ef952515814b549235db6073a9c40a
msgid "5, 6 are Group 2;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-MicoAir743-AIO.rst:74
#: e9eafe69c070419b960e2162d6fb5ec6
msgid "7, 8, 9 are Group 3;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-MicoAir743-AIO.rst:76
#: d5ce77799a134932a7f07dcecf93476d
msgid "PWM1-4 are internally tied to the 4-in-1 ESC. PWM 9 is labeled as LED output on the board."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-MicoAir743-AIO.rst:79
#: ff6d1acbe6994faebbe8099da96e5846
msgid "Battery Monitoring"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-MicoAir743-AIO.rst:80
#: b37d96926917495ab65f646843d67de1
msgid "The board has internal voltage and current sensors for the battery. The voltage input is compatible with 3~6S LiPo batteries."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-MicoAir743-AIO.rst:83
#: 892bb41c879b4fe6a8615acf55db2f94
msgid "The default battery parameters are:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-MicoAir743-AIO.rst:85
#: e96171fe77954e939b0ab215049ef630
msgid ":ref:`BATT_MONITOR<BATT_MONITOR>` = 4"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-MicoAir743-AIO.rst:86
#: a8f5f5dc707f43c8bf1678a9edee1ad5
msgid ":ref:`BATT_VOLT_PIN<BATT_VOLT_PIN__AP_BattMonitor_Analog>` = 10"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-MicoAir743-AIO.rst:87
#: b1e7273014f24cbfb7af6879e073f00d
msgid ":ref:`BATT_CURR_PIN<BATT_CURR_PIN__AP_BattMonitor_Analog>` = 11"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-MicoAir743-AIO.rst:88
#: aeab9513f2d9437e9f95fd127753f93c
msgid ":ref:`BATT_VOLT_MULT<BATT_VOLT_MULT__AP_BattMonitor_Analog>` = 21.2"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-MicoAir743-AIO.rst:89
#: 367b0723dc9d4fd4b4f216d7dae2dd44
msgid ":ref:`BATT_AMP_PERVLT<BATT_AMP_PERVLT__AP_BattMonitor_Analog>` = 14.14"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-MicoAir743-AIO.rst:92
#: a8bc2e5831c14ee2abbe6da013af73b7
msgid "Compass"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-MicoAir743-AIO.rst:93
#: ba5d2dc6b55343d9a3e065c1d8b0499a
msgid "The MicoAir743-AIO does not have a built-in compass, but you can attach an external compass using I2C on the SDA and SCL connector."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-MicoAir743-AIO.rst:97
#: 31adf0eb63d4497a828e78cc70ae9271
msgid "Firmware"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-MicoAir743-AIO.rst:98
#: 6523ad74ebef4089aa4f3e00635f273e
msgid "Firmware for this board can be found `here <firmware.ardupilot.org>`_ in sub-folders labeled “MicoAir743-AIO”."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-MicoAir743-AIO.rst:101
#: 4b6b29eed5fb4d9b8fa3481b8a5c71d0
msgid "Loading Firmware"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-MicoAir743-AIO.rst:103
#: 5b04d30f37844013bbed7dfe2b0ecbb7
msgid "Initial firmware load can be done with DFU by plugging in USB with the bootloader button pressed. Then you should load the \"\\*xxxxx_with_bl.hex\" firmware, using your favorite DFU loading tool."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-MicoAir743-AIO.rst:105
#: 2cd1637fff61468cb387ebeaa4d0634b
msgid "Once the initial firmware is loaded you can update the firmware using any ArduPilot ground station software. Updates should be done with the \"\\*.apj\" firmware files."
msgstr ""
